  "outcome": "needs_user_info",
  "reply_to_user": "Hi Sofia, sorry you missed the Q4 planning invite. I checked and nothing from you is stuck in the spam filter, your account is active and your mailbox has plenty of space, so I don't see a problem on our side. To track this down, could you tell me: 1) Who sent the invite? 2) Does anyone else manage your calendar for you, such as an assistant or delegate? 3) Can you find the invite or meeting in Outlook on the web (outlook.office.com), even if it's not in the desktop app? In the meantime, the quickest fix is to ask the organizer to send the invite to you again. If they do and it still doesn't arrive, let me know and we'll look into it further.",
  "internal_note": "KB-012 checks: lookup_user shows Sofia Rossi (user 7, Marketing) with an active account. Mailbox is 27.9% used, so it isn't a quota problem. Spam quarantine is empty, so the invite was not quarantined and there is nothing to release. I have no tool to check delegate settings or compare the web and desktop views, so I asked the user about a delegate, whether the invite shows in Outlook on the web (if only desktop is wrong, follow KB-009), and who the organizer is. I also suggested asking the organizer to resend. Escalate to Tier 2 if invites from one specific internal organizer never arrive (possible mail rule or transport issue, per KB-012).",
